#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/doc/webgpu-pbr-dev.md:19
msgid ""
"`ActorColorOptions` in `wgsl/ActorColorOptions.wgsl` mirrors "
"`vtkWebGPUActorInternals::ActorBlock::ColorOptions`. The C++ structure is "
"checked against the WGSL layout with `static_assert`s: vec3 members are 16 "
"byte aligned in WGSL, so every vec3 is followed by a scalar or explicit "
"padding in C++. When adding a field, keep both declarations in the same "
"order and update the size assertion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/doc/webgpu-pbr-dev.md:27
msgid ""
"`vtkWebGPUActorInternals::GetPBRTextures()` returns the property textures "
"sampled by the shading, in a fixed order (base color, ORM, emissive, normal, "
"anisotropy, coat normal). Both the actor bind group and the WGSL "
"declarations of the mapper are built from it, so they cannot disagree. "
"Textures with `UseSRGBColorSpaceOn()` use an sRGB format and are decoded by "
"the hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/doc/webgpu-pbr-dev.md:34
msgid ""
"`vtkWebGPURenderer::UpdateEnvironmentMap()` uploads the environment texture "
"and calls `vtkWebGPUEnvironmentMap::Update()`, which regenerates the "
"textures only when the environment changed. The compute shaders live in "
"`wgsl/IBL*.wgsl`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/doc/webgpu-pbr-dev.md:38
msgid ""
"`IBLEnvironmentCube.wgsl` converts the source, a cube map or an "
"equirectangular image, into a RGBA16Float cube map and fills its mip chain. "
"Cube map sources are remapped with the environment basis (right, up, right x "
"up) like `vtkPBRPrefilterTexture` does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/doc/webgpu-pbr-dev.md:41
msgid ""
"`IBLPrefilter.wgsl` prefilters the cube with GGX importance sampling. Level "
"`i` holds roughness `i / levels`, and the shading samples it at `roughness * "
"(levels - 1)`, as the OpenGL backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/doc/webgpu-pbr-dev.md:43
msgid ""
"`IBLIrradiance.wgsl` and `IBLSphericalHarmonics.wgsl` compute the diffuse "
"irradiance as a cube map and as nine spherical harmonics coefficients "
"premultiplied for a Lambertian lobe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/doc/webgpu-pbr-dev.md:45
msgid "`IBLBRDFLookupTable.wgsl` computes the split-sum lookup table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/doc/webgpu-pbr-dev.md:47
msgid ""
"The environment is looked up in world space with `environment_rotation * "
"transpose(mat3(scene_transform.view))`, where `environment_rotation` holds "
"the transpose of `vtkRenderer::GetEnvironmentRotationMatrix()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/doc/webgpu-pbr-dev.md:51
msgid "Shader assembly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/doc/webgpu-pbr-dev.md:53
msgid ""
"The WGSL functions shared by every PBR pipeline are in `wgsl/"
"PBRFunctions.wgsl`. They take two structures, `PBRSurface` (normal, view "
"vector and tangent frame) and `PBRMaterial` (albedo, metallic, roughness, "
"Fresnel terms, anisotropy and clear coat). Keeping the BRDF behind these "
"structures is what allows replacing them with Slang interfaces later without "
"touching the mapper."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/doc/webgpu-pbr-dev.md:58
msgid ""
"`vtkWebGPUPolyDataMapper::ReplaceFragmentShaderLights` builds the body of "
"the fragment shader with `BuildPBRLightingSource()`. What changes the "
"bindings is specialized at compile time: image based lighting, tangents and "
"each material texture. What only changes values is a run time branch on the "
"actor uniforms, because a mapper builds one pipeline shared by all the "
"actors that render it: clear coat and anisotropy are enabled when their "
"strength is not zero. `GetShadingFeatures()` packs the compile time choices "
"into a key, and the pipelines are rebuilt when the key of an actor changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/doc/webgpu-pbr-dev.md:65
msgid "Debugging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/doc/webgpu-pbr-dev.md:67
msgid ""
"`VTK_WEBGPU_PBR_DUMP_DIR=<directory>` writes the generated lookup table, the "
"irradiance and prefilter cube faces as PFM images and the spherical "
"harmonics coefficients as text, every time the environment textures are "
"regenerated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/doc/webgpu-pbr-dev.md:70
msgid ""
"`vtkWebGPURenderer::SetPBRDebugView()` displays one input or term of the "
"shading instead of the shaded color: albedo, normal, roughness, metallic, "
"ambient occlusion, emissive, F0, N.V, direct lighting, diffuse or specular "
"image based lighting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/doc/webgpu-pbr-dev.md:73
msgid ""
"WGSL compilation errors and warnings are logged with the offending line and "
"its neighbors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/WebGPU/doc/webgpu-pbr-dev.md:74
msgid ""
"Every compute and render pass of the environment generation has a label, "
"visible in GPU capture tools such as RenderDoc or the Xcode frame debugger."
msgstr ""
